KEY IDEA (easy memory):
OOP -> model the WORLD as objects (who does what) — mutable state inside objects
FP  -> model the LOGIC as functions (what to compute) — prefer immutable data, no side effects

Java reality (interview tip):
Java is MULTI-PARADIGM — you use BOTH.
Domain model = OOP (Order, User, Service classes)
Data pipelines / transformations = FP (streams, lambdas)


🧠 Quick Summary
